  "verbalization": "Marsdenoside K appears to exert its biological effects through a shared target pathway involving 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which ultimately targets SMMC-7721. This relationship is supported by multiple evidence chains, all of which link Marsdenoside K to a common intermediate, 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, and then to SMMC-7721. The varying scores across the paths suggest that the strength of the relationship may depend on the specific context or experimental conditions, but the core mechanism remains consistent. The presence of multiple targets in the pathway, including MOVP-3 and Carboxylesterase 2, indicates that Marsdenoside K may act through different mechanisms, possibly by modulating the activity of these enzymes or by directly interacting with the chromenone compound. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Marsdenoside K in influencing cellular processes in SMMC-7721 cells, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise mechanism of action.",
